CloudBurrow patch 1 of 1 to github.com/goccy/go-googlesql v0.3.0
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bug: #989).

The bug: the bridge between Go and the WebAssembly GoogleSQL engine sliced
Go's view of wasm memory with int32 addresses (googlesql.go, Module.invoke
and the callback and type-name paths). WebAssembly addresses are unsigned
32-bit, so once the engine's heap grew past 2 GiB an address was negative as
an int32 and every call that used one panicked, "slice bounds out of range
[-2147355456:]", which exited the emulator. The fix converts each address to
uint32 before slicing. wasm_high_address_test.go panics without the fix and
passes with it.

